{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain` to define its node-identity type. Its\nerror type is introduced in {cite}`requirements.sdk.errors`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The one testable obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types` is that an application domain implements `Domain` with a `NodeId` type bounded by `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. The cited `requirements.sdk.errors` and `requirements.sdk.domain` supply context only.\n\n**Bound enforcement.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` is marked as a test of this requirement. It has two parts:\n- The fixture `Relationships` sets `NodeId = Identity`. `Identity` derives only `Clone, PartialEq, Eq` and has no `Debug`, `Hash` or `Ord`. If the trait added a bound beyond those, the fixture would stop compiling.\n- The generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` calls `identity::<G::NodeId>()`, and `identity` requires `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. If the trait dropped any of the four bounds, `check_bounds` would stop compiling.\n\nTogether these catch both loosened and tightened bounds. A compile-time check is the right way to test a trait-bound obligation.\n\n**Behavioral use of `NodeId`.** Several other marked tests exercise `Eq` and `Clone` on node identities at runtime:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` uses an enum `NodeId`. It asserts `assert_ne!` between identities of different variants and compares dependency node identities. It also stores and loads evidence keyed by `NodeId` equality.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` and `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` use a real `HabeasNode` domain.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain]` also covers a real domain.\n- The `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` and `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` tests use `Node` and `Application` domains.\n\nNo gap is found, and no acknowledgments are needed.",
